WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.680
Good morning John,

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.480
I'd like to make a quick logical argument,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.120
two postulates, followed by a conclusion

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.660
Postulate 1:

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.840
creating is terrifying.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.200
postulate 2:

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.840
everyone creates.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.300
logical conclusion then, being,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.640
that everyone is terrified.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.020
It's actually not creating that's terrifying.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.060
It's-It's sharing the creation, or even the thought

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.460
of sharing the creation that's terrifying.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.400
Because once your creation is in front of another person, you have lost all power.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.920
You've gone from a situation in which you have maximum amount of power

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.420
over this thing that you have made,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.860
to no power.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.820
You have nothing.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.700
That's not true, actually.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.700
You have all of your hopes,

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:45.520
and dreams, and values, and aspirations, and days or weeks, or months, or years, of work

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.420
that you've poured into this thing.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.880
That you're now sharing with the world,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.400
and the world has every right to despise.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:52.900
So, yeah,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.820
terrifying, right? Now onto the second postulate.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
That all people are creators.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.180
And now we've sort of been set up to believe that this isn't necessarily the case,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.840
that we live in a world where Steve Jobs makes an iPod and we buy an iPod.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:10.800
But that's not how the world is, even if you have no way of physically creating a thing,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.420
you create ideas, and you create jokes, and you create friendships.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.020
And then, you have the creation that matters most to all of us,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:23.580
and that is the scariest, and most dangerous, and most intimate, and most beautiful creation

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.780
that everybody gets to make.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.760
And you only get to make one of them.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.240
And that's the self.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.700
This is why I totally hate it when people give the advice to just be yourself

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.700
Because, like, who is that?!

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.960
Because we aren't born with a self.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.280
We create ourselves.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.200
You make you!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.700
You make you out of the books that you read,

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.560
and the expectations of culture.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.480
The interactions with your friends and your family,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.920
and a million other factors.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.640
And because the self is this terrible, intense creation,

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.580
and the most important creation that we all make

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.740
When someone tells you that they don't like that thing,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.340
that's terrible.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.680
Which is why talking to a stranger is always scary, like, to me anyways

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.140
I don't know, I feel like everybody must feel like this to some extent.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.320
Because when you talk to a new person,

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.260
you are making you,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.940
inside of them.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.760
And you don't wanna do a bad job.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.580
And that's why we all fear judgment so much. Because judgment

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:21.580
is just someone creating you inside of their head without your permission, without full knowledge of who you are.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.340
They're making you, but they're making you improperly. It's terrifying.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.420
That's absolutely terrifying.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.980
There are a few ways that I've found to make it less terrifying.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.720
You can create the bare minimum of creation,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.500
you can not try very hard.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.120
That's good.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.960
You can be really bland, you can just create really bland

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.260
things that look like everything else that everyone else has ever created,

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.760
or you can create things that you don't care about at all.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.000
Or for people who you don't care about

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.320
Or, you can just never ever share the things that you create

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.420
And, of course, all of theses strategies, are terrible ways to live

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.540
It's terrible to see people doing this with their creations

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.520
But the most terrible creation to see people do this with

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.620
is their self.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:05.520
Trying to be boring, trying to look like everyone else, or worse, not trying at all

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.460
Which has led me to the belief

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.700
that you know, as the creator, how worthwhile your creation is

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.720
by how terrified you are.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.000
I've only ever found one solution to this, which is just to create

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.060
To create in spite of fear and to create constantly

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.800
To create for children and adults, and your parents, and your idols, and your peers, and your community

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.880
and to consciously be creating yourself

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.100
everyday

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.400
to make you the you that you feel best inside of

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.380
And create friendships,

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.620
because I honestly believe that friends are the commodity by which we should all be judged.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.280
It's the only way that I've found to temper the fear of creation

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.960
Just to create, constantly.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.600
Because, to be clear, the fear doesn't go away

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.120
You just get more comfortable in it.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.520
John, I'll see you on tuesday

